# pa-framework public repo: whitelist-style exclude file.
# Default: ignore EVERY top-level entry. Then un-ignore the substrate paths.

/*

# Re-include public substrate at the root
!/.gitignore
!/.gitignore-public
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/.env.example
!/config.example.yaml
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/pa/
!/projects/

# Inside projects/: ignore everything except the public-facing subtrees
projects/*
!projects/telegram-bot/
!projects/daily-mail-brief/
!projects/google-oauth-redirect/
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/
!projects/reminders/

# Inside pa/: exclude personal/build/private artifacts
pa/data/
pa/.claude-needs-brain
pa/dist/
pa/node_modules/
pa/src/oracle_agent.py
pa/src/active_mail.py
pa/src/learn_agent.py
pa/src/travel_butler.py
pa/src/gmail_utils.py
pa/src/telegram_notify.py
pa/scripts/backup_fitness.py
# Python tests for the excluded modules above — they import learn_agent/
# telegram_notify, which don't exist in the public mirror (permanently-broken
# tests there), and their fixtures/docstrings reference personal context.
pa/src/tests/
pa/scripts/tests/test_telegram_notify_429.py
pa/scripts/memory_consolidation.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_memory_consolidation.py
# Tests importing the private modules above — CI unittest-discover dies on them
pa/scripts/tests/test_unconfirmed_facts.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_start_google_telegram_reauth.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_reservation_guard.py
pa/scripts/migrate_profile_metadata.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_migrate_profile_metadata.py
pa/scripts/profile_repair.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_profile_repair.py
pa/scripts/rotate_secrets.py
pa/scripts/tests/test_rotate_secrets.py
pa/scripts/upload_apk.py
# pa/scripts/run_restore_drill.py — INCLUDED (monthly backup integrity check)
# pa/scripts/tests/test_run_restore_drill.py — INCLUDED
# pa/scripts/redteam_injection.py — INCLUDED (monthly injection regression tests)
# pa/scripts/tests/test_redteam_injection.py — INCLUDED
# pa/scripts/run_eval.py — INCLUDED (self-improver eval gate)
# pa/scripts/upload_plan.py — INCLUDED (refactored to env-driven via PA_PLANS_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID; see Cat E3)

# Inside projects/telegram-bot/: exclude build/state/runtime artifacts + personal prompt
projects/telegram-bot/dist/
projects/telegram-bot/node_modules/
# Private planning docs must never reach the public mirror (any project subtree)
projects/*/plans/
# Compiled .js artifacts that belong in dist/, not src/ (catches accidental tsc output in source dirs)
projects/telegram-bot/src/*.js
projects/telegram-bot/src/tests/*.js
projects/telegram-bot/.claude-needs-brain
projects/telegram-bot/bot-instructions.md
projects/telegram-bot/run-bot-hidden.vbs
projects/telegram-bot/test_repro.mjs
projects/telegram-bot/src/tests/apply-teardown-guard.ps1

# Inside projects/daily-mail-brief/: track only scripts + README + requirements + config template
projects/daily-mail-brief/*
!projects/daily-mail-brief/README.md
!projects/daily-mail-brief/requirements.txt
!projects/daily-mail-brief/config.example.json
!projects/daily-mail-brief/scripts/
# Exclude personal one-off email helpers (hardcoded recipient/subject/body)
projects/daily-mail-brief/scripts/draft_reply.py

# Inside projects/whatsapp-drafts/: track code, docs, tests, and example contact data
projects/whatsapp-drafts/*
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/README.md
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/INSTRUCTIONS.md
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/scripts/
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/tests/
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/data/
projects/whatsapp-drafts/data/*
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/data/README.md
!projects/whatsapp-drafts/data/contacts.example.json

# Inside projects/reminders/: track code, docs, and tests
projects/reminders/*
!projects/reminders/README.md
!projects/reminders/add_reminder.py
!projects/reminders/process_reminders.py
!projects/reminders/tests/

# Inside projects/google-oauth-redirect/: exclude the deployment-specific
# bot-username config (names the bot; config.example.js stays tracked).
projects/google-oauth-redirect/config.js

# Universal noise excludes
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# === Repo hygiene patterns (mirror of private .gitignore — see docs/CONVENTIONS.md) ===
# Scratch and WIP — never tracked publicly
**/scratch/
**/temp_*.py
**/temp_*.json
**/temp_*.md
**/temp_*.txt
**/debug_*.py
**/debug_*.log
**/*-debug.log
**/test_repro.*
**/test_real_login.*

# LLM-agentic scratch writes at repo root (see private .gitignore for detail).
# /output.md + /error_log.txt added 2026-07-21 after the same failure mode
# recurred under new names (a full daily-brief body; a one-line provider error).
# /oracle_output.txt added 2026-08-08 (same class — real personal/financial
# content this time, see private .gitignore for the full incident note).
# **/glm-[0-9]* added 2026-08-13: zclaude (GLM models) writes its response to
# a model-named file at cwd (glm-4.7, glm-5.2[1m], root and subdirs).
/message_to_user.md
/output.json
/output.md
/skill_proposals.json
/error_log.txt
/oracle_output.txt
**/glm-[0-9]*

# Project data subdirectories (each project keeps its own data outside the repo)
**/data/raw/
**/data/processed/
**/data/exports/

# Claude Code session config — deployment-specific. The thin delegation skills
# under .claude/skills/ (added 2026-08-15) invoke THIS deployment's `pa run`
# git-workflow family; public-mirror users get examples/skills/ instead.
.claude/
